# Deny by default, then allow back exactly what the image needs.
#
# The inverse -- listing what to exclude -- silently starts shipping anything a future directory
# adds, and one of the things this repository can grow is real survey data. data/team.yaml is a
# team's actual answers; baking it into an image that gets pushed to a registry would be the
# worst failure available here. So: nothing is in the build context unless it is named below.
*

# The package and its metadata. README.md and LICENSE are not documentation here -- hatchling
# reads both out of pyproject.toml during the install and fails without them.
!pyproject.toml
!requirements-dev.txt
!README.md
!LICENSE
!src/

# The interface, the example team, and the local Streamlit settings.
!app/
!data/team.example.yaml
!.streamlit/

# Re-exclude what would otherwise ride along inside the directories allowed above.
**/__pycache__/
**/*.py[cod]
.streamlit/secrets.toml
